            <ArticleTitle>Tungsten-rhenium thin film thermocouples for SiC-based ceramic matrix composites.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>015007</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1063/1.4973967</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A tungsten-rhenium thin film thermocouple is designed and fabricated, depending on the principle of thermal-electric effect caused by the high temperature. The characteristics of thin film thermocouples in different temperatures are investigated via numerical analysis and analog simulation. The working mechanism and thermo-electric features of the thermocouples are analyzed depending on the simulation results. Then the thin film thermocouples are fabricated and calibrated. The calibration results show that the thin film thermocouples based on the tungsten-rhenium material achieve ideal static characteristics and work well in the practical applications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
